---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Home" active="Home">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <h1 class="hero-name">Abhishek Karna</h1>
        <p class="hero-role">PhD Student in Theoretical Physics</p>
        <p class="hero-affil">Princeton University</p>
        <nav class="hero-links">
          <a href="mailto:akarna.work@gmail.com">
            <i class="fas fa-envelope"></i> Email
          </a>
          <span class="sep">/</span>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/abhishekkarna/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <i class="fab fa-linkedin"></i> LinkedIn
          </a>
          <span class="sep">/</span>
          <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=fF3vhcEAAAAJ&hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <i class="fas fa-graduation-cap"></i> Scholar
          </a>
          <span class="sep">/</span>
          <a href="/resume.pdf" target="_blank">
            <i class="fas fa-file-pdf"></i> CV
          </a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About -->
  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <p>
        I'm a <span class="brush">PhD student in Theoretical Physics at Princeton</span>, working on quantum
        condensed matter physics. My current research applies machine learning to quantum materials. I use it to
        classify, predict, and screen for properties that are hard to compute from first principles alone.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before Princeton, I spent four years at Duke doing a bit of everything: building new <span class="brush"><a href="https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/gtbl-vsdt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quantum
        Monte Carlo algorithms for quantum spin systems</a></span>, growing <a href="/projects/APS Global Physics Summit - Karna, Abhishek - 2025.pdf" target="_blank">single crystals in a furnace</a>, and modeling
        <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apr.2026.102920" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">pollution in the Indo-Gangetic region</a>. I graduated with a Bachelor of Science in Physics, a Bachelor of Science
        in Mathematics, and a Certificate in Philosophy, Politics, and Economics (PPE). I also wrote a <a href="/projects/MycoPoetica - Karna, Abhishek - 2022.pdf" target="_blank">poetry
        collection about fungi</a> and documented <a href="https://duke.is/m/nax2" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">temples across South Asia and Southeast Asia</a>. The common thread,
        if there is one, is a preference for questions that resist clean disciplinary labels.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Featured Publication -->
  <section class="featured-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Featured Publication</span>
      <div class="pub-featured-card">
        <span class="pub-status-tag">Published &mdash; Physical Review D 113, 074511 (2026)</span>
        <h3>Projected Density Matrix Sampling for Lattice Hamiltonians</h3>
        <p class="pub-authors">
          <strong>Abhishek Karna</strong>, Hansen S. Wu, Shailesh Chandrasekharan, Ribhu K. Kaul
        </p>
        <p class="pub-meta-line">arXiv:2511.19209 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; April 2026</p>
        <p class="pub-abstract">
          We present a continuous-time path-integral Monte Carlo method for computing the low-lying spectrum of
          generic quantum Hamiltonians within a projection subspace. The method is free of Trotter discretization
          errors and converges systematically to low-energy states with finite overlap with the projection subspace
          as &beta; increases. Applied to the 1D Ising model near the E&#8328; critical point and the frustrated
          Shastry&ndash;Sutherland model, demonstrating quantum Monte Carlo spectroscopy for lattice Hamiltonians.
        </p>
        <div class="pub-action-links">
          <a href="https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/gtbl-vsdt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary">
            <i class="fas fa-external-link-alt"></i> Physical Review D
          </a>
          <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.19209" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn">
            <i class="fas fa-file-alt"></i> arXiv
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
